---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '@components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, legal } from '@config/site';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Evidence Axis handles the limited information you share through website inquiries, complimentary brief requests, email and business correspondence."
  path="/privacy/"
  noindex={false}
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy" meta={[`Last updated ${legal.lastUpdated}`]} />

  <section class="section container">
    <div class="legal measure">
      <p class="legal__intro">
        This note explains what information {site.name} receives through this website and business
        correspondence, and how that information is used. Any paid engagement is also governed by the
        terms agreed for that specific project.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is operated publicly by {legal.publicOperator}, whose legal name is
        {' '}{legal.operatorLegalName}. Privacy questions can be sent to
        {' '}<a href="mailto:hello@evidenceaxis.com">hello@evidenceaxis.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If an engagement is contracted through {legal.internationalInvoicingEntity}, that company
        may also receive the client and transaction details needed to contract, invoice, keep
        business records and deliver the work. The applicable contracting party is identified in
        writing before paid work begins.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you provide</h2>
      <p>
        If you request a Complimentary Competitive Intelligence Brief, use the website inquiry form,
        or contact us by email, we receive the details you choose to send. These may include your
        name, work email, company, company website, role, decision or research question, named competitors
        and related context. We use this information to verify the business request, understand the
        research context, respond to the inquiry and, where requested, prepare the relevant work.
      </p>

      <h2>Work-email and company verification</h2>
      <p>
        A Complimentary Brief is available to verified company employees using a work email. We may
        compare the email domain, company name and company website, or manually review a mismatch, to
        reduce impersonation, spam and other abuse. This verification is used to validate the request;
        it is not sold or used for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Business correspondence</h2>
      <p>
        If we correspond about a possible or active engagement, we keep the information reasonably
        needed to carry out and account for that work. We do not sell it, and we do not use it for
        advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Technical information</h2>
      <p>
        Basic technical information (such as standard server request data) may be processed to keep
        the site available and secure. The current site does not use advertising trackers or advertising
        cookies. Website inquiry submissions are transmitted through FormSubmit for delivery to our
        business inbox. If analytics, Gift-view tracking or additional cookies are introduced, this
        notice will be updated and consent will be requested where required.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Service providers may process limited information where needed for website hosting, email,
        form delivery, file storage, invoicing or delivery. They are given only the information needed for that
        function and remain subject to their own security, privacy and legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep inquiry and engagement information for as long as reasonably necessary for the
        purpose it was provided, and for legitimate business and record-keeping needs, then remove
        it. If you would like your inquiry information removed, email
        {' '}<a href="mailto:hello@evidenceaxis.com">hello@evidenceaxis.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what inquiry information we hold about you and request that it be corrected or
        removed. Depending on your location, additional rights may apply; we will honor applicable
        requirements. Requests can be sent to the email address below.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or privacy requests can be sent to
        {' '}<a href="mailto:hello@evidenceaxis.com">hello@evidenceaxis.com</a>. Postal correspondence
        concerning an engagement should be sent to the contracting address stated in that
        engagement's written terms or invoice.
      </p>

      <p class="legal__foot mono">Last updated {legal.lastUpdated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal__intro { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--text); }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--space-xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
    padding-top: var(--space-s); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .legal p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); }
  .legal__foot { margin-top: var(--space-xl); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-faint); }
</style>
